  "note": "Nomination-day report for the twenty-six electoral divisions of Magherafelt rural district, one member each. Twenty-five candidates were returned unopposed; James Henderson withdrew from Tobermore, leaving John Colhoun returned. Gulladuff alone was contested, on 30 May 1924. M'Cann (Nationalist), 248; Boyle (Unionist), 218; majority 30."
